From 3ab4df277b5aa922b379156ddb350073f3024175 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: c6 <c6@localhost>
Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 22:00:50 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 11/11] c6: slices 'T[:]' with bounds checking

Add a slice view type 'T[:]': two machine words '{ T *const data; const
size_t len; }' with a fixed layout (data at 0, len at PTR_SIZE) that
libtcc1 and every translation unit agree on, so a slice can be passed
to and returned from another unit by just writing 'T[:]' on both
sides.  The internal struct is built by hand rather than through
struct_layout(), so #pragma pack cannot change the ABI.

'T[:]' is read where a type specifier is expected.  A '[' directly
after a type specifier is not valid C (array declarators come after
the name), so only '[:]' is claimed: 'int a[3]', 'int a[] = {..}',
'void f(int[])' and 'typedef int T[]' keep their meaning, and
'int[3] x;' stays the syntax error it always was.

Arrays convert to slices implicitly in run time contexts (assignment,
initializer, argument, return, explicit cast), an array decay giving
'{ &a[0], N }'.  A static initializer has no code to run, so it must
spell the fields out: 'int[:] g = { a, N };'.  's[i]' checks 'i < len'
and 's[lo:hi]' checks 'lo <= hi <= len' before touching memory; a
violation traps the same way an unproven 'catch' body does, since
libtcc1 is freestanding and has no diagnostics channel.  '.data' is
the unchecked escape hatch (C pointers), '.len' the length.

Slices are views: no ownership, no cap, no append, no copying.  The
element type must be a complete object type whose struct/union/enum
tag is at file scope (a tag declared inside a function dies with the
block, the slice type lives until the end of the unit); top level
qualifiers on the element are dropped -- the slice header itself is
const, which is what prevents rebinding it.

Tests: 175 covers arrays, ranges, struct/array/char elements, function
parameters and results, struct members, typdefs, compound literals,
size and alignment; 176 checks the diagnostics; 177 passes and
returns slices across two units.  tests2 156/156 with C6_EXT,
134/134 without.
